---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "A store miss under write-no-allocate leaves the cache empty, so a load of the same line misses too and reads the stored value from memory (cases 9 and 2)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | memWrite | allocatePolicy | memory 0xA4, writearounds | - | Write-no-allocate: 7 goes straight to memory at 0x0A4. The cache is unchanged.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
2.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
2.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (7) into r1.
